1272
00:54:32.330 --> 00:54:36.850
For the movies in the grief counseling session, I was really excited.

1273
00:54:37.170 --> 00:54:38.530
It was really fun to think about.

1274
00:54:38.530 --> 00:54:44.150
I went off on script and needed to find a way that everybody would sit there with Michael

1275
00:54:44.150 --> 00:54:51.210
Scott and not share their own personal stories of huge loss because it just didn't seem like

1276
00:54:51.210 --> 00:54:51.970
they would do that.

1277
00:54:51.970 --> 00:54:58.170
So I thought they should share movies, plot lines as if they were their own lives.

1278
00:54:58.270 --> 00:55:07.690
And I came up with Million Dollar Baby for you, Jennifer, Pam, and then also for Kevin, Weekend

1279
00:55:07.690 --> 00:55:08.330
at Bernie's.

1280
00:55:08.650 --> 00:55:11.350
And for Ryan, I had a different one.

1281
00:55:11.570 --> 00:55:14.210
I think BJ came up with The Lion King.

1282
00:55:14.210 --> 00:55:16.390
I don't quite remember, but I think it was BJ.

1283
00:55:16.390 --> 00:55:17.870
And I love that one.

1284
00:55:18.510 --> 00:55:22.030
The one I had, I actually found my first draft of the script.

1285
00:55:22.510 --> 00:55:24.910
I had Ryan, I'll read you the line.

1286
00:55:25.130 --> 00:55:29.170
It's not as good as The Lion King one, but I have Ryan say, this is almost too horrible

1287
00:55:29.170 --> 00:55:33.370
to talk about, but I had a cousin who was a big city lawyer and he was visiting an Amish

1288
00:55:33.370 --> 00:55:34.590
town not far from here.

1289
00:55:34.710 --> 00:55:36.870
And he was smothered to death in their grain silo.

1290
00:55:37.270 --> 00:55:39.930
And then I had Michael say, ooh, that must've made you really sad.

1291
00:55:39.930 --> 00:55:40.330
Did it?

1292
00:55:40.410 --> 00:55:41.270
And Ryan says, yes.

1293
00:55:41.270 --> 00:55:44.330
So I think that was a witness.

1294
00:55:44.570 --> 00:55:45.630
So I had Ryan's from witness.

1295
00:55:45.690 --> 00:55:49.770
I wish I could remember some of the other ones because I feel like we had other ones

1296
00:55:49.770 --> 00:55:53.190
that we pitched on, but those were the ones from my first draft.

1297
00:55:53.370 --> 00:55:56.010
And then of course, The Lion King Circle of Life was fantastic.

1298
00:55:56.250 --> 00:56:00.450
And Ryan saying, it'll take about an hour and a half to tell it was like such a great

1299
00:56:00.450 --> 00:56:00.730
line.

1300
00:56:01.690 --> 00:56:02.910
That is amazing.

1301
00:56:03.130 --> 00:56:06.630
By the way, my college roommate and I used to watch witness and we would say to each

1302
00:56:06.630 --> 00:56:09.490
other all the time, be careful out among them English.

1303
00:56:10.750 --> 00:56:11.570
Thank you.

1304
00:56:11.850 --> 00:56:14.510
That is my movie quote from witness.

1305
00:56:14.950 --> 00:56:19.170
But isn't that wild, Jenna, that Ryan's movie went through three versions.

1306
00:56:19.390 --> 00:56:23.030
It was witness and then it was, I guess, Thelma and Louise, according to your script.

1307
00:56:23.370 --> 00:56:25.750
But The Lion King is what made it in the show.

1308
00:56:26.610 --> 00:56:33.870
Yeah, clearly they had a lot of alts for these movie plots, but all of them were scripted,

1309
00:56:33.990 --> 00:56:34.150
guys.

1310
00:56:34.390 --> 00:56:36.290
All of them written by our awesome writers.

1311
00:56:36.510 --> 00:56:38.050
We did not improvise that stuff.

1312
00:56:38.050 --> 00:56:39.290
Love that.

1313
00:56:39.430 --> 00:56:41.370
Love that little tidbit, Jen Salata.

1314
00:56:41.850 --> 00:56:47.510
So guys, Michael gets pretty upset that people are not taking this seriously.

1315
00:56:48.050 --> 00:56:54.170
